<title>INDIA: India's SEBI approves new foreign investors.</title>
<headline>India's SEBI approves new foreign investors.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) said on Wednesday it has registered 16 new foreign institutional investors (FIIs) taking the total to 412 from 396 previously.</p>
<p>It said net FII investments in Indian stock markets during October 1-11 was $67.3 million against $122.8 million for the whole of September.</p>
<p>SEBI said cumulative FII inflows since India allowed foreign portfolio investments totalled $6.86 billion as on October 11, 1996.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
